      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess it comes down to \"For still (non-animated) image codecs, this will return an empty vector\" not being obviously clear. Is a GIF image with 1 frame still or animated? Does the answer change if we\u0027re incrementally decoding and it\u0027s \"a GIF image with 1 frame *so far*\"? It would be weird if onGetFrameInfo(0, nullptr) returned true at some point but, after further incremental decoding, returned false.\n\nThis conversation sounded familiar. It turns out that I had previously proposed a longer comment. See patch set 1 of https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/146021/1..3\n\nHeh. So, I think the src/codec implementations (and libgifcodec, which lives outside src/codec) are working as intended, and \"frameInfos.empty()\" is a sufficient *but not necessary* condition for stillImage-ness (meaning that the pixels do not change over time, as opposed to animated-ness).\n\nThis patch to tools/convert-to-nia.cpp is therefore still applicable. Specifically, if a BMP image is losslessly convertible to a GIF image (i.e. 256 or fewer colors), then the one-step conversion BMP -\u003e NIA should be equivalent to the two-step conversion BMP -\u003e GIF -\u003e NIA, even though frameInfos.empty() would be true for BMP and false for GIF. In both cases, though, both of these are true:\n- frameCount \u003c\u003d 1\n- frameInfos.size() \u003c\u003d 1\n\nShould this CL be further updated so that the modified non-comment line becomes \"bool stillImage \u003d frameCount \u003c\u003d 1\"?\n\nOr, perhaps, remove the stillImage variable and use getFrameInfo(int, FrameInfo*) further below instead of getFrameInfo()?\n\nSeparately, I\u0027ll try to re-draft the SkCodec::getFrameInfo() comments from that patch set 1 referenced above, and send out a new comment-only CL to include/codec/SkCodec.h. WDYT?",
